# Project rules (always apply)

Source of truth: `docs/SPEC.md`. Build order is Part E of that file, or `docs/AUTOPILOT.md` when a run is started with it. Package name: `hubvik`. Read the spec before any task.

## Never
- Never create, read, print or store npm/GitHub tokens or `.npmrc` auth lines.
- Never run `npm publish` or `npm login` in the terminal. The GitHub release workflow publishes. If the npm website then shows the version as staged, the person clicks Approve there. Do not stop in Cursor to ask for that click.
- Never add a runtime dependency to `packages/core`. `dependencies` must stay `{}`. devDependencies go in the repo root only.
- Never change a detector threshold, default, severity or formula without updating `docs/SPEC.md` in the same commit and noting it in `CHANGELOG.md`.
- Never weaken, skip (`test.skip`, `todo`) or delete a failing test to make a gate pass. Fix the code, or stop and report.
- Never block, drop or modify traffic. The library only reports.
- Never invent facts in docs (detection rates, benchmarks, dataset results). Only publish numbers produced by scripts in this repo.

## Always
- Node ≥ 22, CommonJS (`'use strict'`), JSDoc on every public function, `.d.ts` kept in sync.
- One detector = one file `packages/core/src/detectors/<id>.js` + one test file `packages/core/test/detectors/<id>.test.js`.
- Every detector test covers: fires on attack · silent on 14-day benign traffic for every simulated device class · respects caps · survives export/import · (hard rules) fires during learning.
- Deterministic tests: seeded PRNG from `test/fixtures/prng.js`. No `Date.now()` or `Math.random()` in tests.
- Bounded memory: every Set/Map/array that grows with traffic has a cap from options and a test that hits it.
- Validate all external input (events, options, baselines, indicators). Reject `__proto__`, `constructor`, `prototype` keys.
- Small commits, conventional messages: `feat(detector): horizontal-scan`, `fix(engine): flush closes only ended windows`.
- After every task, `npm run gate` must be green before a commit is pushed. `npm run check` is lint, types, and tests. It is not the gate.
- When that gate exits 0 on the release tree, commit `release: x.y.z` on `release/<x.y.z>`, push that branch and tag `v<x.y.z>`, and merge into main after the GitHub workflows are green. Do not ask. Do not run `npm publish` or `npm login`.
- When the spec is ambiguous or seems wrong: stop, write the question in `docs/QUESTIONS.md`, and ask. Do not guess silently.
